      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "When you call the [`bestMoveForActivePlayer()`](gkstrategist/bestmoveforactiveplayer().md) method, the Monte Carlo strategist randomly chooses between the available moves for the current player (see the [`gameModelUpdates(for:)`](gkgamemodel/gamemodelupdates(for:).md) method of your game model class), then randomly chooses a subsequent move, and so on, until it reaches a state in which the game is either won or lost.",
      "normalizedSource": "When you call the [`bestMoveForActivePlayer()`](gkstrategist/bestmoveforactiveplayer().md) method, the Monte Carlo strategist randomly chooses between the available moves for the current player (see the [`gameModelUpdates(for:)`](gkgamemodel/gamemodelupdates(for:).md) method of your game model class), then randomly chooses a subsequent move, and so on, until it reaches a state in which the game is either won or lost.",
      "sourceHash": "92ab06ae70d9c880ccdc3fddc79ba82ec7783d19ac75d64a74e54315bc7bc474",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "Then it returns to the original game state and repeats that process, accumulating information about which sequences of moves are more or less likely to result in a win.",
